# Copy this file to `local.properties` (same directory) and fill in your own
# API key values. Your real `local.properties` is gitignored — keys you put
# there will never be committed.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Get a Google Cloud API key. Enable "Maps SDK for Android",
#      "Places API (New)", and "Places API" (legacy) on the project.
#   2. Get an OpenWeatherMap API key from https://openweathermap.org
#      (newly created keys take up to 2 hours to activate).
#   3. Copy this file to `local.properties` and replace the empty values below.
#   4. In Android Studio: File -> Sync Project with Gradle Files, then Run.
#
# Note: Android Studio may have already created a `local.properties` for you
# with `sdk.dir=...`. If so, just append the two API key lines below to it.

sdk.dir=
MAPS_API_KEY=
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=
